From: Hanna Jose <hjose@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 08:57:49 +0000
Subject: [Description]:Improves dnsmasq lease cleanup and ARP/neighbor-state handling to avoid stale disconnected-client entries.
Adds safe IPv4 validation and explicit unreachable-state support for robust lease release decisions.

[RCA/Root Cause Analysis]: Disconnected clients could disappear from ip nei while lease entries persisted in dnsmasq.leases.
Limited state parsing and missing validation caused stale IP/MAC records and inconsistent host/lease sync behavior.

[Fix Description]:Added releaseIPOnDisconnect() to iterate dnsmasq leases, verify presence in neighbor states, and run dhcp_release when absent. Extended neighbor states (DELAY/PROBE/UNREACHABLE), added IPv4 validation, and integrated release path into Hosts_SyncArp().

Signed-off-by: Hanna Jose <hjose@qti.qualcomm.com>
